  "query_preview": "Forecast... With a front stalled north of the \narea, scattered showers and storms are anticipated Monday afternoon \ninto the night with brief periods of MVFR or IFR restrictions \npossible. As on Sunday, the highest convective coverage is expected \nacross northern-NC TAF sites (KLBT, KILM). Storm chances decrease on \nTuesday, leaving a low risk for transient MVFR or IFR restrictions \nin convection. Thunderstorm coverage is expected to increase \nWednesday into Thursday as a stronger cold front approaches, \nbringing a greater potential for widespread storms and associated \nrestrictions Wednesday and Thursday.",
